  "body": "## Source-only HOLD \u2014 do not merge or deploy\n\nThe Chairman's Sovereign Auction and Funding Pressure program needs an auditable auction context view without adding unvalidated auction fields to Mastermind decision inputs. The existing stored-plane route would affect coverage and prompts, so this change enriches only the served Market View response.\n\n### Changes\n\n- Read Macro's existing `event_calendar.json` nested context through the existing feeds contract, with strict point-in-time, instrument, lifecycle, null and authority validation.\n- Add one separate section to the existing Market View page. EN/ZH, light/dark, exact dollar formatting, future-first grouping, bounded expansion and explicit unknown/source-failure states are supported.\n- Retain raw source evidence in native disclosures. Correct the new expander's grid placement and the inherited narrow-screen panel containment issue.\n- Preserve stored bytes, coverage, tilt, decision-context assembly, prompt summary, PM enrichment and legacy crash-leg authority.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- **26 native reader/API tests passed**, with actual FastAPI dependencies; actual page-script renderer assertions passed.\n- **48/48 actual HTTP/Chromium cases passed**, spanning three sizes, EN/ZH, light/dark and four source states. Final source disclosures are explicitly opened and checked.\n- The real four-source fixture contains **74 observed episodes**; synthetic failure cases are declared separately. Final screenshots were inspected.\n- Exact final hashes and complete receipts are in `research/sovereign_auction_context/VERIFIED_SOURCE_MANIFEST.json` and `verification/browser_final/`.\n- Start with [`SOURCE_DELIVERY.md`](https://github.com/mastermindx-market-intelligence/Mastermind/blob/8b74970c13a8915097d0d9e5849499904c1fcc2b/research/sovereign_auction_context/SOURCE_DELIVERY.md). Earlier candidate manifests/reviews remain historical records.\n\n### Boundaries and integration\n\nMacro **#8657** owns data, lifecycle, economic primitives, research and the source publication bridge. The current checkout's absent/dangling vendor path was not repointed to fixtures. Local delivery simulation and the real route harness do not establish production deployment, provider/lifespan execution, auth, actual vendor refresh or predictive validity.\n\nNo probability, risk gate, sizing, exit policy, `auction_stress` or `treasury_auctions` alias is added. Existing null studies and decision-owner authority remain intact. Independent source/CI review and separately authorized production readback are still required.\n",
